.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt REQUEST_MEM_REGION 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm request_mem_region
.Nd reserve an MMIO range in the global resource tree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/resource.h
.Ft "struct resource *"
.Fn request_mem_region "resource_size_t start" "resource_size_t n" "const char *name"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn request_mem_region
function reserves a memory-mapped I/O range in the global resource tree.
Conflicting reservations fail.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn request_mem_region
function returns the reserved resource on success or
.Dv NULL
on conflict or allocation failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr resource 9 ,
.Xr ioremap 9
